From 2db2e617ce0ee5543ad46acc7a8ef80a9e5b24df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Mario=20B=C4=83l=C4=83nic=C4=83?=
 <mariobalanica02@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Jun 2024 02:36:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] feat(rk3588): introduce SD/MMC Control Service
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The whole point of this service is to allow the Windows SD/eMMC drivers
to effortlessly control necessary clocks and voltages, since this is all
done in non-standard ways via CRU and a PMIC on the SPI bus.

Why not use ACPI methods?

We want to be able to collect crash dumps when SD/eMMC is used as a boot
drive. The crash dump stack is much more limited and does not provide
any means to call into the ACPI driver.

Change-Id: I2b51f787a5255b2a30a6a5ec14f00031f351e6b2
Signed-off-by: Mario Bălănică <mariobalanica02@gmail.com>
---
